{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/577478-too-much-family-consequences-of-beast-populations","id":577478,"title":"Too Much Family-Consequences of Beast Populations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-03T10:41:34-07:00","id":577478,"title":"Too Much Family-Consequences of Beast Populations","content":"I hate population discussions. It really is a matter of how many of a supernatural you want in a given area.<br /> <br /> Except, of course, it matters when you're thinking both about the 'ecological' consequences of a population in a given area, or when you're planning a revolutionary game, and what else are you going to do in Paris with Beasts? But this is me thinking way ahead in advance-though it also gives us frame of reference, so without going into the story specifics, let's use Paris as a petri dish to explore the question of what we think the effects would be of certain Beast populations within a given area.<br /> <br /> The Paris Metropolitan Area in the year 2011(Great, I'm planning around that year!) was measured to be about 17,174 km\u00b2 with a population of 12,292,895 people. As a rule for supernatural populations in large cities, I use a rule of starting at 300 as a baseline, and then shift as I think is appropriate for the template and the city*. In our case, we'll posit that this is the Mid-High range of the population of Paris, and the low end is 50. Soooo, that means the table for density looks something like this:<br /> <br /> Low Population: 50 Beasts, or 1 Beast for every 343.48 square kilometers<br /> Mid-Low Population: 134 Beasts, or 1 Beast for every 128.16 square kilometers<br /> Mid Population: 216 Beasts, or 1 Beast for every 79.5 square kilometers<br /> Mid-High Population: 300 Beasts, or 1 Beast for every 57.25 square kilometers<br /> High Population: 383 Beasts, or 1 Beast for every 44.84 square kilometers<br /> <br /> Not even a drop in the bucket, but that's not accounting for a lot of factors, so we'll leave it be for now.(Or, rather, you can discuss them yourself)<br /> <br /> So, what's the level of effect each tier of Beast population density do you think would have on Paris, and if you think it's negligible even at the highest population suggestion here, suggest how much you'd think it'd start making an effect.<br /> <br /> I don't need an overstuffed population for the purposes of the game idea I have in mind, but population densities do matter for revolutions as well as probable Hero populations, so, yeah.<br /> <br /> *While this clearly doesn't apply to all types, like Prometheans or Mummies, it does also set a neat precendent for how many supernaturals are in Paris, with about 3000 in the Metro Area, give or take a few hundred for reduced populations of some groups, glutted populations of others, and of the decently large smattering of lesser templates. That's not even 1 percent of the population, so I might tweak the rule here after hearing some input on the effect of Beasts at the proposed levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:56:25-07:00","id":577571,"title":"","content":"There's going to be a biiig pile of dishes to clean up after that family dinner!<br /> <br /> But speaking seriously. I think there's a lot more pertinent factors to consider with Beasts than with Vampires over the consequences of their feeding. Because the effects may vary greatly based on the type of Hunger the majority has and their associations with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I know this isn't what you were asking, but yeah. &lt;,&lt;<br /> <br /> What I mean by it is! It seem to me the effects of Beasts on the populace are a lot more flexible than what you'd think only based on population density comparisons. So there's a good deal of freedom to determine the sort of influence their presence has on the rest of Paris even within the same level of population.<br /> <br /> Though, that aside. Higher numbers of Beasts obviously mean higher numbers of Heroes... or rather they mean higher number of Heroes drawn to hunt Beasts and possibly getting into tussles with other supernaturals. But ponder the following! Maybe there's a smaller number of 'sleeping' Heroes in Paris than in most places. Or maybe there's a very big number of them; maybe there's a sizeable difference between Heroes and Beasts, for better and for worse. Less Heroes certainly means the Beasts have more lease to indulge their Hungers, to teach their lessons. But if there are more Heroes, maybe Beasts aren't the only pie they have their hands on. Especially if many of the Beasts associate themselves with groups of other supernaturals. Perhaps there are others who have their hands in <i>the Heroes' pie </i>even, for a myriad of reasons.*<br /> <br /> I'm babbling at this point, but I hope you get something useful out of that!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Most of what I say in this paragraph is assuming you're following the revised version, if that wasn't clear. I mean, I dunno, some people may like the status quo and implications of the original kickstarter preview better.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-03-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T12:52:47-07:00","id":577635,"title":"","content":"This also depends on what type of supernatural has highest population rate in paris and what they think of the other supernatural also have considered who the apex of paris is and what he thinks of the city as well as what effects he has on the hive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T13:12:40-07:00","id":577647,"title":"","content":"That is a thing I don't know yet. I'm tempted to say changelings, but their Bulwark is fairly solid, so the number of abductions is not quite big enough to warrant a major power state. the next three contenders I see are Vampires, Werewolves, and Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T13:21:12-07:00","id":577656,"title":"","content":"So changelings can set up Bulwarks to keep people from being kidnapped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T13:39:30-07:00","id":577669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/577478-too-much-family-consequences-of-beast-populations?p=577656#post577656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So changelings can set up Bulwarks to keep people from being kidnapped?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope so - it can create interesting plot dilemmas. Especially if the bulwark involves something either very difficult or morally troubling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T13:43:25-07:00","id":577696,"title":"","content":"There are also New Orleans numbers in Beast corebook, in background section of SAS The Morning After:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Whole World of Darkness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This method requires some work, both in terms of setup and for the Storyteller to keep the game from devolving into madness, but it can be very rewarding. In this method, the World of Darkness is an integrated whole \u2014 New Orleans has a vampire population (perhaps the one described in the <b>City of the Damned: New Orleans</b> sourcebook, perhaps not), but also plays host to werewolves, mages, changelings, and whatever else you want to throw into the mix. Sure, that might strain credulity, but a) we\u2019re talking about a game in which the players take on the roles of nightmare monsters from the Primordial Dream and b) New Orleans is a big city. The metro area has a population of roughly 1.2 million, and that\u2019s not including visitors. If .5% of that population is in some way touched by the supernatural, that\u2019s still 6000 people (or \u201cpeople,\u201d anyway). That\u2019s more than enough for several otherworldly populations to be represented.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re going this route, think about where the points of conflict are, who the movers and shakers are, and where the Beasts fit in. Pay closest attention to the French Quarter, since that\u2019s where the action takes place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those numbers may seem too much. But buddy of mine pointer that \u201ctouched by supernatural\u201d does not mean our main lines monsters. If we assume that all the Lesser Templates and various \u201cother\u201d monsters are in ratio 3:1 to Major Templates, then we end with 1500 proper lines monsters in New Orelean metro area - it\u2019s raughlty 150 member per race. Let\u2019s screw a numbers in favor of Kindred ( it is \u201ctheir\u201d city in sourcebooks ) and we will end with something like 500 vampires, 100 werewolves, 70 mages, 20 prometheans, 200 changelings, 100 hunters, 200 Sin-Eaters, 10 mumies, 50 demons and 250 beasts. I think those numbers are really okay, seeing how supernatural societies works in World of Darkness. Just remeber for your city building that you look more for the 0.0125% rather for your Major Templates population. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2015, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:00:38-07:00","id":577801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/577478-too-much-family-consequences-of-beast-populations?p=577656#post577656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So changelings can set up Bulwarks to keep people from being kidnapped?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, this is the point of the Bulwark in fluff. While the mechanics don't support it, it's been in the spirit of the text given in Court Creation that the True Fae have a harder time just waltzing in.<br /> <br /> But even if you go strictly by the mechanics, the fact of the matter is that Paris, for all the bumps it's had getting here and some of the inherent ricketyness of the Bulwark, the Rose Freehold is pretty well manned and directed and does okay with it's resources. What that translates out to mechanically for the Freehold is that True Fae who venture out and run into a Parisian patrol is going to have problems with the Bulwark in effect. The Huntsmen, Privateers, and Loyalists have to confront the fact that Paris is also fairly tightly knit for a large freehold thanks to the Courted system, so despite all the problem Paris has, so long as they follow the Bulwark, they have a fairly tough system to crack. Have that system apply to defending the system and keeping watch, and of course less people are going to be kidnapped on average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:01:46-07:00","id":577803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/577478-too-much-family-consequences-of-beast-populations?p=577696#post577696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also New Orleans numbers in Beast corebook, in background section of SAS The Morning After:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Those numbers may seem too much. But buddy of mine pointer that \u201ctouched by supernatural\u201d does not mean out main lines monsters. If we assume that all the Lesser Templates and various \u201cother\u201d monsters are in ratio 3:1 to Major Templates, then we end with 1500 proper lines monsters in New Orelean metro area - it\u2019s raughlty 150 member per race. Let\u2019s screw a numbers in favor of Kindred ( it is \u201ctheir\u201d city in sourcebooks ) and we will end with something like 500 vampires, 100 werewolves, 70 mages, 20 prometheans, 200 changelings, 100 hunters, 200 Sin-Eaters, 10 mumies, 50 demons and 250 beasts. I think those numbers are really okay, seeing how supernatural societies works in World of Darkness. Just remeber for your city building that you look more for the 0.0125% rather for your Major Templates population. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, damn, that's very useful. Thank you Wyrd!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:20:06-07:00","id":577832,"title":"","content":"I would say sin eater should be the biggest in. number especially in a revolution game mostly because its been pointed out in mortal remains that whenever war violence or even large amounts of death occurs the sin eater number increases","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T16:52:14-07:00","id":577953,"title":"","content":"It's only the Beasts who are having a Revolution, though the supernatural family is at stake, so fringes will come in.<br /> <br /> The build up to the crossover game is somewhat multiversial, in my head. If I can make it universal, I will, but if stuff doesn't line up, that happens.<br /> <br /> Still, the Sin-Eaters were the way I was angling. Paris's history is stained black with all manner of death, and if that's not precedent for a significant Conspiracy, I don't know what does. PLus I like the premise of death-demigods in Paris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T03:06:11-07:00","id":641310,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;250 Shades of Horror&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It does have a nice ring to it, doesn't it? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T09:24:37-07:00","id":641727,"title":"","content":"I think the only unifying impact Beast populations have on the world around that is that in order to feed, something must be fed on. Beasts actively make the world around them worse. The more Tyrants you have running companies, the more it begins to function a a dystopic corporate-ran wasteland. The more eshmaki you have around, the more dangerous it is to go out at night. However, because of the Beast's nature this also shapes what people learn. In the eshmaki example, not only would more bad things happen to people who wlalk home alone in the dark, more people would <i>know</i> that as an understood. They wouldn't walk home in the dark unless they were brave, foolish, or careless (to varying degrees) and in need of a reminder.<br /> <br /> Also, wow. Even if we do 0.1% of the population as a Major template, that's still 12,292 major supernaturals. 3,000 Vampires, 2,000 Werewolves, 2,000 Sin Eaters, 2,000 Changelings, 1,000 Beasts, 1,000 Mages, 1,000 Demons (actually Demon and Angel Covers, exact number of Angels and Demons unknown), 25 Prometheans, 10 Mummies... still not at the cap. The thing is, I don't like exorcises like these. I can't fathom having to create a political structure with 3,000 people. I'd subdivide the city, paint it in broad strokes, and flesh out a small number of people in a more contained area. You can have beautiful New York game set entirely in Manhattan and not feel claustrophobic, for instance. It also tries to boil down the supernatural into a statistic. Prometheans and Mummies in particular shouldn't be a statistic but a wonderous and miraculous event. There's also the oddity that suddenly supernatural populations are slashed by the thousands every time a new splat comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T09:58:14-07:00","id":641756,"title":"","content":"I usually stick to 1 in 10k or less. So for my Chicago setting there are 200~250 vampires. Since I want less Werewolves, Mages, and Changelings I use numbers like 1 in 30k, 1 in 50k and 1 in 20k. For really rare things like Prometheans, Mummies, and Beasts, I go 1 in 100k each. It all really depends on the kind of stories you want to tell and what kind of crossovers you expect to support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T17:25:04-07:00","id":642203,"title":"","content":"Well, there are three things that Beasts primarily do - seek out other supernaturals (negligable effect on Paris as a whole), fight heroes and hunters (generally reactive, again minimal), and feed their Hungers (now we're talking). <br /> <br /> Hoard. Ruin. Prey. Power. Punishment. At low Satiety feedings, its not a big ripple effect. Maybe come off as bit of a jerk in public. Dominance games in line at the grocery store, pick pocketing, punching someone that annoys you. At high Satiety, most beasts live off Family Dinner. <br /> <br /> The big events are when Beasts fall into Ravening, and must evoke a Satiety potential 8 event. Can you imagine the Ruin? We're talking massive damage. Hoard has to steal something worth a lot. These are the massive events that will have I'm not sure will have the big problems. I'm not sure how often a Begotten will fall to that level, but its more than possible, and potentially disasterous for the city when it happens. Each time when it happens, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}